##-- Output configuration ----------------

## For more details read `man 5 sway-output`
## You can get a list of output names with: swaymsg -t get_outputs

## Set wallpaper on all monitors
output * bg /home/anthony/.config/sway/wallpapers/wallpaper.jpg fill

## Set wallpaper on specific monitors
#output eDP-1    bg ~/.config/sway/wallpapers/wallpaper.jpg fill
#output HDMI-A-1 bg ~/Pictures/wallpapers/wallpaper_2.jpg fill

## Multiheads
#~ Laptop screen (internal monitor), mode: 1920x1080
#output eDP-1 resolution 1920x1080 position 0,0
#~ External monitor, right of laptop screen, mode: 1920x1080
#output HDMI-A-1 resolution 1920x1080 position 1920,0
#~ And just like above (working) examples, you can setup your monitors here.

## HiDPI
#~ Internal monitor with default scale
#output eDP-1 scale 1
#~ External monitor with twice scale
#output HDMI-A-1 scale 2

## HiDPI Laptop
#output eDP-1 mode 2944x1840@90Hz
#output eDP-1 position 0,0
#output eDP-1 scale 1.7
#output eDP-1 scale_filter smart

## Persistent monitor layout -- "work" profile (Y-shape): Dell + LG side by
## side above, laptop centered below. Mirrors bspwm's work-layout.sh, but
## using wlroots output scaling (1.5x on the LG) instead of xrandr's
## resolution downscale to land the LG's native 4K panel on the same
## logical 2560x1440 as the Dell, so the two sit top-aligned side by side.
##
## Matched by make/model/serial (from `swaymsg -t get_outputs`) rather
## than port name -- same reasoning as bsp-assign-desktops' EDID matching,
## and the same identifiers the $laptop/$dell/$lg workspace-output
## bindings further down in ~/.config/sway/config use (duplicated here
## rather than shared, since this file is included before those variables
## are defined).
##
## This is also the actual fix for displays reverting to some
## auto-negotiated default after every theme change: theme.sh's apply_sway
## calls `swaymsg reload` on every theme switch, and sway only preserves
## whatever the config file says to reapply for each output. A layout set
## live via the Displays app but never written here doesn't survive that
## reload -- these lines are what make it survive.
output "Dell Inc. DELL S2725DS C6N6614" mode 2560x1440@59.951Hz position 0 0 scale 1
output "LG Electronics LG HDR 4K 0x00000939" mode 3840x2160@59.997Hz position 2560 0 scale 1.5
output "AU Optronics 0xF99B Unknown" mode 1920x1200@60.026Hz position 1758 1439 scale 1
